Aeneas patch of the krepi proof tools.

Base: Aeneas commit 4acbb6d73abe9082e45cf49ba6d6229a2c7d5836 of
https://github.com/AeneasVerif/aeneas. Apply it in the root of that tree with
`git apply`, which skips this text before the first file header.

The patch changes the Lean backend only:

1. A call of `Option<&mut T>::unwrap`, where `T` holds no borrow, translates
   to `core.option.Option.unwrap.mut`, a definition that the patch adds to
   the Aeneas Lean library. It returns the payload together with a backward
   function, as `core.result.Result.unwrap.mut` does for
   `Result<&mut T, E>::unwrap`. Every other shape keeps the existing
   translation.
2. A generated name counts as taken when another generated name extends it
   by a `.` component, so that no definition shares its name with the
   namespace of another one.

Origin: ported from cas-project@f2d2fba26cbf09474e6df8e59650014ae58dec78,
file `verification/tooling/aeneas-option-unwrap-mut-and-prefix.patch` (SHA-256
e12c89822e366d99c37850218d9d0d6155bcf88ebb3e1db2f8d70ddb793bde3e), which was
written for Aeneas commit d119a474f852781f8ae88a85424f2f8ba8407b82. The port
differs only in the hunk of `backends/lean/Aeneas/Std/Core/Core.lean`: the
hunk starts at line 75, and the binders of its context and of the added
definition read `{T : Type _}`, as upstream commit
6c2788d1366f09d69fd55b2b9be71cd17d28a9ab changed them. The other seven
hunks are unchanged.

